#!/usr/bin/env perl

use v5.42;
use warnings;
use App::fdimg;

# PODNAME: fdimg
# ABSTRACT: Create and inspect raw DOS FAT12 floppy images
# VERSION

exit App::fdimg->main(@ARGV);

__END__

=head1 SYNOPSIS

 fdimg create utilities/
 fdimg create utilities/ release/disk1.img
 fdimg create --format auto-1200k --force utilities/
 fdimg create --label UTILITIES --exclude '*.bak' utilities/
 fdimg create --no-label --no-follow-symlinks utilities/
 fdimg create --empty --format 360k disk.img

 fdimg info disk.img
 fdimg ls -r disk.img
 fdimg extract disk.img unpacked/
 fdimg validate disk.img
 fdimg formats
 fdimg completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/fdimg

=head1 DESCRIPTION

B<fdimg> creates raw (uncompressed sector dump) DOS FAT12 floppy images
from a directory of DOS software, suitable for copying to a
Gotek/FlashFloppy USB stick, using in an emulator, or producing in a
release pipeline.  It needs no root privileges, mounting or loop devices.
It is a thin interface to L<Disk::Diskette>.

=head1 REQUIREMENTS

The mtools programs (C<mformat>, C<mcopy>, C<mmd>) must be installed and
in C<PATH>, for example with C<apt install mtools>, C<dnf install mtools>
or C<brew install mtools>.  Your own mtools configuration is ignored.

=head1 COMMANDS

=head2 create

 fdimg create [options] SOURCE [IMAGE]
 fdimg create --empty [options] IMAGE

Copies the SOURCE directory into a new image.  IMAGE defaults to the
source path with C<.img> appended (C<utilities/> becomes
C<utilities.img>), and must not be inside the source tree.  On success
the actual format is reported, for example
C<Created utilities.img (720K FAT12)>.

Host file and directory names must already be legal DOS 8.3 names; case
is ignored and names are stored in uppercase.  Nothing is truncated or
renamed and no long file names are created: an illegal name, or two
names that are the same ignoring case, is an error.  Entries whose
names start with C<.> are ignored.

Options:

=over 4

=item --format, -f FORMAT

A fixed format (C<160k>, C<180k>, C<320k>, C<360k>, C<720k>, C<1200k>,
C<1440k>, C<2880k>) or automatic selector (C<auto-360k>, C<auto-720k>,
C<auto-1200k>, C<auto-1440k>, C<auto-2880k>).  Automatic selectors pick
the smallest format in the drive family that fits; the default is
C<auto-1440k> (720k or 1440k).  See C<fdimg formats>.

=item --label, -l LABEL

Volume label (up to 11 characters; stored in uppercase).  The default is
the uppercase source directory name.

=item --no-label

Create an unlabeled image.

=item --follow-symlinks, --no-follow-symlinks

Symlinks to regular files are followed by default, and each is copied
as an independent file under the link's name.  C<--no-follow-symlinks>
makes every symlink an error.  Note that link targets may be outside the
source tree.

=item --exclude PATTERN

Exclude paths matching a shell-style glob.  A pattern without C</>
matches a basename at any depth; one with C</> matches the whole
source-relative path (a leading C</> anchors to the source root).
Repeat the option for several patterns; together they replace any
configured list.  Quote patterns so your shell does not expand them.

=item --config PATH, --no-config

Read configuration from PATH instead of the source's C<.fdimg.toml>, or
read no configuration.

=item --force

Replace an existing image atomically.  Without it an existing image is
an error.

=item --empty

Create an empty, formatted image; IMAGE is required and
source-specific options are rejected.

=back

=head2 info

 fdimg info IMAGE

Format, geometry, filesystem layout, volume label, serial number, raw
size and free capacity.

=head2 ls

 fdimg ls [--recursive|-r] IMAGE [DIR]

Lists a directory (the root by default) with attributes, size and
modification time (UTC).

=head2 extract

 fdimg extract IMAGE DEST

Extracts the image into the host directory DEST (created if needed).
Nothing is ever overwritten: if any file would be, nothing is
extracted.

=head2 validate

 fdimg validate IMAGE

Checks the geometry, boot sector, FATs and directory structure, and
reports every problem found.

=head2 formats

 fdimg formats

Lists fixed formats and automatic selectors with their candidates.

=head2 completions

 fdimg completions bash|zsh|fish

Prints a completion script for the given shell.

=head2 help

 fdimg help [COMMAND]

=head1 CONFIGURATION

A C<.fdimg.toml> file in the root of the source directory (and only
there) supplies defaults.  It is never copied into the image.

 format = "auto-1440k"
 label = "UTILITIES"
 follow_symlinks = true
 exclude = ["README.md", "*.bak"]

Command line options override configuration per setting.
C<label = ""> requests an unlabeled image.  Unknown keys and invalid
values are errors.

=head1 ENVIRONMENT

=over 4

=item SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

When set, enables reproducible mode: file timestamps are clamped to this
time, directories and the volume label use it, and the volume serial
number is the low 32 bits of the epoch.

=back

=head1 EXIT STATUS

C<0> on success (including help and version), C<1> if the operation
failed, C<2> for a command line usage error.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<Disk::Diskette>

=cut
